bin/

# Timestamped intermediate runs are noise — regenerate them with `make all`.
bench/results/bench_*.txt
bench/results/scaling_*.txt
bench/results/hyperfine_*.json
bench/results/latest.txt

# Profiles are large and machine-specific; the extracted -top text is the
# evidence the report actually cites, so that stays.
bench/profiles/*.pprof
bench/profiles/*.svg

# Everything else under bench/ and docs/env/ is COMMITTED on purpose:
#   bench/results/baseline.txt   the v0 "before" column of every comparison
#   bench/results/benchstat.txt  the statistical comparison
#   bench/results/hyperfine.md   the whole-binary timings
#   bench/profiles/*.top.txt     the hot-path evidence
#   docs/env/*.txt               the bench machine specification (rubric §1)
# The rubric treats this repo as "pièce à conviction" for the measurements.
# Ignoring the measurements would defeat the point.

# Supports de cours (PDF) — exclus du depot PUBLIC.
# Ce sont les documents pedagogiques de l'intervenant (christophe-lecroq.dev).
# Les rediffuser publiquement releve de son droit d'auteur, pas du notre.
# Ils restent presents en local ; voir docs/README.md.
docs/*.pdf
